Fixed: the DNS 💡 hint now matches the error text reqwest actually produces. That was committed as f61f588b with Fixes #1126 in the title. On this resume the working tree is clean, and formatting, clippy with -D warnings, and the full cargo test (all 34 test suites) pass.

The bug: diagnose_api_error only looked for "dns resolution failed" and "name resolution failed". The real text, captured on Day 248, is ConnectError("dns error", … "failed to lookup address information: Name or service not known"), which contains neither. So a DNS failure retried 6 times and ended with no hint.

The fix (in `src/prompt_retry.rs`): the network-error check now also matches "dns error" and "failed to lookup address information". I widened "name resolution failed" to "name resolution" so the Linux temporary-failure wording ("Temporary failure in name resolution") matches too. The hint is produced the same way as before, so -p mode still leaves out the REPL-only /retry line.

Before and after on the built binary, using --base-url http://no-such-host-yoyo-probe-4821.com -p hi:
• Before: (failed after 6 attempts) and no 💡 line.
• After: 💡 Network error — could not reach the API.

Tests are in a new sibling file, src/prompt_retry_dns_tests.rs, so prompt_retry.rs itself stays small:
• They reuse the captured REAL error text rather than retyping it. I made that constant test-only and crate-visible, and made the reserved_dns module crate-visible; no logic changed.
• They cover the real reqwest text, the macOS and Linux resolver wordings, and both old spellings, and they compare the whole hint string, not just whether a hint came back.
• Two near-miss cases: "Connection refused" still gets exactly the hint it got before, and "image resolution too large" gets no network hint.
• The old answer-key test is unchanged.
• Reserved names like .invalid and .test still fail fast through their own path, so they don't get a second hint.

Checking the tests catch the bug: with the three new matches disabled, the two new tests failed by name. With them restored, all three passed, in one command.

The size cap for prompt_retry.rs in tests/module_size.rs went from 2787 to 2793, with a comment naming #1126. I didn't touch the REPL-style wording of the billing and model hints; that's #1128.
